<!-- ==================== PAGE 8: FEASIBILITY STUDY & NEED ==================== -->
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always" />

<h2>2.2 Feasibility Study</h2>
<p>
    • <strong>Technical Feasibility:</strong> The architecture is constructed using lightweight, native web standards (HTML5/CSS3/ES6+ JavaScript). It requires zero server runtimes, functioning reliably on budget smartphones and low-bandwidth connections. The print engine outputs directly to standard A4 sheets.<br>
    • <strong>Economic Feasibility:</strong> Built with open-source tools and hosted free of charge on GitHub Pages, the project has zero operational expenditure while delivering immense economic savings to micro-entrepreneurs.<br>
    • <strong>Operational Feasibility:</strong> Features an accessible visual layout with interactive touch sliders and pre-set prompt chips requiring no formal financial literacy.
</p>

<h2>2.3 Need and Significance of the Project</h2>
<p>
    Over 70.0% of Indian micro-enterprises currently borrow from unorganised moneylenders at exorbitant interest rates (24.0% to 60.0% per annum). Samarth Business directly equips them with the documentation required to secure institutional bank loans at 5.0% to 11.5% interest, aligning with national economic empowerment mandates (Atmanirbhar Bharat, Make in India) and solving Smart India Hackathon Problem Statement <strong>SIH26092</strong>.
</p>
<p class="noindent">
    • <strong>Bridging the Formal Credit Chasm:</strong> Facilitates compliant DPR creation, enabling formal loans at concessional interest rates.<br>
    • <strong>Empowerment of Marginalised Cohorts:</strong> Dedicated schemes like Stand-Up India (SC/ST and women borrowers) and PM Vishwakarma (artisans) receive immediate algorithmic matching.<br>
    • <strong>National Vision Alignment:</strong> Directly advances <em>Atmanirbhar Bharat</em>, <em>Digital India</em>, and <em>Make in India</em>.
</p>

<!-- ==================== PAGE 9: 3. METHODOLOGY (PART 1) ==================== -->
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always" />

<h1>3. METHODOLOGY / PLANNING OF WORK</h1>

<h2>3.1 Step-by-Step Approach to Achieve Project Objectives</h2>
<p class="noindent">
    1. <strong>Phase 1: Government Gazette Verification:</strong> Extraction and verification of authentic parameters from the Ministry of MSME, KVIC, DFS, and MoHUA into a normalized JSON store.<br>
    2. <strong>Phase 2: Multi-Page UI Engineering:</strong> Design of `login.html`, `dashboard.html`, and `scheme-detail.html` using responsive FinTech aesthetics.<br>
    3. <strong>Phase 3: Financial Capital Allocation Algorithm:</strong> Mathematical modelling of dynamic capital budgeting for machinery, stock, operating funds, interior, and reserves.<br>
    4. <strong>Phase 4: Bank DPR Synthesis Engine:</strong> Creation of the RBI-compliant Detailed Project Report generator.<br>
    5. <strong>Phase 5: Digital Ledger & Advisory Integration:</strong> Implementation of the Khata ledger and AI Co-Pilot chat module.<br>
    6. <strong>Phase 6: Testing & Quality Assurance:</strong> Cross-browser testing, A4 print calibration, and automated deployment.
</p>

<h2>3.1.1 Mathematical Formulation of Capital Allocation</h2>
<p>
    Let total capital be \(C_{\text{Total}} = C_{\text{Loan}} + C_{\text{Equity}}\). The platform algorithmically segments \(C_{\text{Total}}\) using adaptive trade weights:
</p>

<p class="table-caption">Table 3.1: Dynamic Working Capital Allocation Matrices Across Business Trades</p>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 25%;">Business Trade</th>
            <th style="width: 15%;">Machinery</th>
            <th style="width: 15%;">Stock</th>
            <th style="width: 15%;">Op. Capital</th>
            <th style="width: 15%;">Interior</th>
            <th style="width: 15%;">Contingency</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Retail Grocery / Kirana</strong></td><td>12.0%</td><td>45.0%</td><td>18.0%</td><td>15.0%</td><td>10.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Cloud Kitchen / Food Cart</strong></td><td>38.0%</td><td>20.0%</td><td>18.0%</td><td>14.0%</td><td>10.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fabrication / Light Mfg.</strong></td><td>52.0%</td><td>16.0%</td><td>14.0%</td><td>8.0%</td><td>10.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Garment & Apparel Boutique</strong></td><td>22.0%</td><td>40.0%</td><td>16.0%</td><td>12.0%</td><td>10.0%</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>General Micro-Retail (Default)</strong></td><td>32.0%</td><td>24.0%</td><td>16.0%</td><td>13.0%</td><td>10.0%</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

